course: dictionary
lesson: 15277
title: One word, many meanings: simmering
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. «Mum let the soup simmer for an hour.» Soup cannot be angry, so simmer here means cooking gently in liquid, with small bubbles, just below boiling.
explain: Feelings can simmer too. «Sam said nothing, but his anger was simmering inside him.» Simmering here means a feeling is growing slowly inside someone without fully showing yet. Ask yourself: is this a pan, a feeling, or a problem? The words around it will tell you.
explain: A problem can simmer as well. «The argument between the two teams had been simmering for weeks.» It is quiet for now, but it could grow worse. When someone is calmer after being angry, we say they are simmering down: «Give her a few minutes to simmer down.»
fact: Simmering is gentle cooking in liquid that is just below boiling, with small bubbles.
fact: «Simmer» is slower and gentler than «boil»: a boiling pot bubbles hard and fast.
fact: A feeling that is simmering is growing inside someone without fully showing yet.
fact: A problem that is simmering is quiet for now, but it may get worse.
fact: «Simmering down» means becoming calmer after being angry or excited.
exercise: «The sauce was simmering gently on the stove.» What is the sauce doing? | Boiling hard, with huge bubbles everywhere | *Cooking gently, with small bubbles | Frozen solid in the pan | Cooling down in the fridge
exercise: «Tom said nothing, but his anger was simmering inside him.» What does simmering show? | Tom falling asleep | *A feeling growing inside without fully showing yet | A feeling that has fully exploded | Tom feeling cold
exercise: Which phrase means becoming calmer after being angry? | Boiling over | Freezing up | *Simmering down | Bubbling up
test: «The argument had been simmering for weeks, and now it was getting worse.» What does simmering mean here? | *Quiet for now but likely to grow worse | Cooked in a pan | Finished and forgotten | Happy and friendly
test: «Keep the heat low so the soup just simmers, and do not let it boil.» What does simmers mean in this sentence? | *Cooks gently in liquid just below boiling | Freezes solid | Is poured into a cup | Cooks fast in a rolling boil
exam: «After the shouting stopped, Mum's voice was calm, because she had simmered down.» What does simmered down mean? | Got louder and angrier | Left the room in a hurry | *Became calmer after being angry | Cooked the dinner more slowly
